# tally 2.2 (CHANGES.md 2.2-11, pick P26). An ask's register doesn't depend on the asks before it: e2 pins the def
# copy wc to the read of wb, so nothing reads wa under the pin and e2 names wb alone, run after e1 or alone (L §8.2:
# an entry is listed exactly when a read in its set gives it). refcore kept e1's carried names across asks.
# tally 2.3 (G1, #247): a window that reaches a move's `on` or `at` makes it a hole day (L §4.4 A movement takes a
# day, §5.14): the movement's places are the hole on every day, HOLE-IMPRECISE naming the day; re-stored.
=== m.tally
model g4_pin_copy3
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "G4 review: a def copy wc of a window wa, pinned to another window's read wb; only wb is read."

source card "invented"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input pay: money PLN

input wa: date

input wb: date

def wc: date = wa

move pay_a: transfers
  on wc
  leg cash from world to konto amount pay

move pay_b: transfers
  on wb
  leg cash from world to konto amount pay

version v_card
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pay = 100.00 PLN "c"
  wa = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) "c"
  wb = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) "c"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "c"

ask e1: bal(konto, 2026-03-06)
ask e2: bal(konto, 2026-03-06) with wc = wb
=== expect e1 e2
e1: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for the day of pay_a" (wa) ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for the day of pay_b" (wb)
  unknown day: wa
  unknown day: wb
  cut 2026-01-10
e2: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for the day of pay_a" (wb) ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for the day of pay_b" (wb)
  pinned: wc = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07)
  unknown day: wb
  cut 2026-01-10
